Europe includes countries with different welfare systems, labor markets, housing costs, demographic trends, and levels of economic development.

The European Union, the United Kingdom, the Western Balkans, Eastern Europe, and other European regions should not be treated as one uniform economy.

The strategy should therefore distinguish between countries with extensive public services and countries where households have less access to them.

